      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 71-year-old male presented with periumbilical ecchymosis formed after acute onset of abdominal pain and near collapse. At the time of presentation the haematoma was the only symptom. Following a CT scan, the diagnosis of a contained rupture of an iliac artery aneurysm was made. The patient was successfully treated with an endovascular stent graft."},
